{"id":"chatcmpl-56bb07de-e6b2-4316-aa58-7e85e4979643","object":"chat.completion","created":1795229582,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"When multiple vision-language models disagree on a binary medical imaging finding, the successful strategy was to escalate through independent model opinions, targeted region-of-interest zooming, and anatomy-focused re-questioning rather than trusting a single model. The final answer was resolved by majority consensus across three independent VLMs after a focused inspection of the relevant anatomical region. This demonstrates a robust conflict-resolution pattern for ambiguous visual evidence.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When two independent models disagree on a finding, query a third independent model and resolve by majority consensus rather than defaulting to either single opinion.\",\n    \"When a finding is subtle or the view is non-ideal, zoom into the anatomically relevant region (ROI crop) and re-ask a focused question about that region before deciding.\",\n    \"Rephrase verification questions to request anatomical course/description (not just presence/absence), which elicits more informative and discriminative model responses.\",\n    \"Treat model disagreement as a signal to gather more evidence (extra models, zoomed inspection) rather than as a reason to abstain or guess.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Use multiple independent VLMs; on disagreement, add a third opinion and majority-vote. Zoom into the anatomically relevant region and ask for descriptive (course/location) rather than binary answers.\",\n    \"Ambiguous visual evidence\": \"Escalate evidence quality: crop/zoom the region of interest, ask targeted anatomy-specific questions, and combine independent sources before committing to an answer.\",\n    \"Multi-model consensus tasks\": \"Prefer majority consensus across 3+ independent models over any single model; document the conflict and the resolution rationale.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm at least two independent model opinions agree, or obtain a third opinion to break a tie before finalizing.\",\n    \"Verify the finding by inspecting a zoomed crop of the anatomically relevant region and asking a focused, descriptive question.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":841,"total_tokens":1252,"completion_tokens":411,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":841},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":411}}}